A glimpse at two newly announced characters and their devastating weapons.
Warhammer Survivors launches November 10, new characters revealed
Today, we&#8217;re excited to announce that Warhammer Survivors launches on PS5 November 10 . To mark the occasion we’re also revealing two characters in our latest trailer.
Eagle-eyed fans who have been following the game for a while may have noticed Morvenn Vahl in the game&#8217;s key art, and we&#8217;re really excited to show her off in full pixel art glory finally. Warhammer Survivors allows you to play in both the Warhammer 40,000 and Warhammer Age of Sigmar universe, so her counterpart (as part of today&#8217;s reveal) is Lyssa Revenya, a skilled thief and tomb-robber.&nbsp;
As one of our larger Warhammer Survivors characters, Vahl strides across the battlefield in her ornate Paragon Warsuit. She&#8217;s armed with the devastating Heavy Bolter Fidelis, which sprays an arc of projectiles obliterating her foes. The weapon also has a chance to trigger a miracle, blessing Vahl and increasing the weapon&#8217;s rate of fire.&nbsp;
In Warhammer Survivors, Lyssa turns her signature tools for breaking and entering into weapons. The Rope and Grapnel shoot hooks in from random edges of the screen, colliding with specific points on the battlefield, damaging enemies and dragging away any who survive. It&#8217;s the perfect weapon for a nimble thief who likes to stay more than a sword-length from their enemies.&nbsp;
Warhammer Survivors launches on November 10; Morvenn Vahl and Lyssa Revenya are just two of over 40 playable champions waiting for you in-game. You can wishlist and pre-order on PlayStation 5 starting today, and PlayStation Plus members will receive a 10% discount when pre-ordering.
While both champions take prime position in today&#8217;s spotlight, they couldn&#8217;t be more different.&nbsp;
